{
	"_note": "The city's building pool (D-256 Tripo heroes and fillers, D-257 district palettes, D-253 one carve path). Rows by hand: name, district, role (hero or filler), storeys (real-world, from the prompt sheet). tools/landmarks/bake.py --pool fills each row's baked shape: w, d, h (sim units and floors), chunks, kvox, stretch_floor. floors = max(min_floors, round(storeys x tallest_floors / tallest_storeys)): the tallest skyscraper is tallest_floors high, about 2x the adult croc (D-257). districts: the palette each model's colours are graded to at bake time (mix toward the nearest palette tint, dark on all but signs, bright on signs), the town_share range its blocks take in today's city (CityPool), and four palette shifts [hue degrees, saturation, value] a placed copy picks from. placement: see CityPool. A row's floors, when set, overrides the storeys rule: H11, H12, H13 and F33 are shrunk until they fit a block's depth (about 7 units; lead's default A, 2026-10-26); H10, the tallest, is 24 floors so its 6-unit base fits a block. A model is taken out of the game by deleting its row. placement (CityPool): on; hero_chance = chance a block takes a hero (set into a corner, the lots under it give way); share = chance a remaining lot takes a filler; fill_slack = most units a filler may fall short of its lot a side; big_chance = chance a block that draws no hero takes a filler of at least big_side units a side instead (too big for a lot); hero_rise = a block model may be this many times the block's tallest lot; patch_m = the side of the square that takes one district style; reuse_m = no copy of a model within this of another (wider than the adult's game-camera view, about 82 x 58 m, so a model shows at most once a view); max_stretch = most floors a copy adds; a model suits a lot within height_fit x the lot's floors (at least height_fit_min).",
